635 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (A simple twist on Raspberry White Chocolate, but it's just soooo good! A summery flavour staple that I can't get enough of right now. I actually LOVE the fact that these use all white chocolate.  The freeze-dried strawberries and biscuit chunks balance the flavours & sweetness perfectly.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
636 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (The dough is made using the same method as always. I added the freeze-dried strawberries in with the flour mixture as one of the dry ingredients.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
637 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (The only thing I did differently was adding the shortcake biscuits whole. If you crush them beforehand, they're more likely to disintegrate & become another dry ingredient instead of giving you those biscuit chunks throughout the cookie.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 216 0 R
/E (Once the dry ingredients have almost finished mixing in, add the whole shortcake biscuits just before the eggs go in. Your mixer should be strong enough to break them into chunky pieces without turning them into crumbs.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
